# QVAC 0.21 in Expo

Mobile remains deferred. Use the full internal CLI source build, not the minimal public-preview CLI. See `skills/setup-mobile-app/SKILL.md` for commands and acceptance boundaries.

## Two workers

The app calls `@qvac/sdk` through static React Native imports. The SDK starts its own Bare worker. The custom `bare/index.js` worklet owns local storage and any P2P logic you add, and must not import the SDK. Worker readiness does not prove discovery or replication. Worklet IPC and bare-rpc connect that custom worklet to the UI.

## Compatible package set

Use Expo 54, RN 0.81.5, React/React DOM 19.1.0, `react-native-bare-kit@0.15.6`, and `@qvac/sdk@0.21.0`. Kit 0.15.6 embeds Bare 1.33.4; pinning it prevents silent runtime changes. See `core/verified-versions.mdc`.

Select only the capability the app uses:

```json
{
  "plugins": ["@qvac/sdk/llamacpp-completion/plugin"]
}
```

Save this as `qvac.config.json`; Expo uses JSON configuration. In app.json:

```json
{
  "expo": {
    "plugins": [
      ["@qvac/sdk/expo-plugin", { "installMissingPrebuilds": true }],
      "expo-router",
      ["expo-build-properties", { "android": { "minSdkVersion": 29 } }]
    ]
  }
}
```

The plugin bundles and verifies the SDK worker, installs published platform addons and refreshes native linking. Keep a lockfile after prebuild. The custom worklet is bundled separately with `bare-pack --host ios-arm64 --host ios-arm64-simulator --host ios-x64-simulator --host android-arm64 --linked`. Do not move SDK imports into that bundle to avoid maintaining its own bundle.

## Completion

```ts
import { loadModel, completion, QWEN3_5_0_8B_MULTIMODAL_Q4_K_M } from '@qvac/sdk'

const modelId = await loadModel({
  modelSrc: QWEN3_5_0_8B_MULTIMODAL_Q4_K_M,
  modelType: 'llm',
  modelConfig: { ctx_size: 4096, reasoning_budget: 0 },
})

let text = ''
const run = completion({ modelId, history: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Hello' }], stream: true })
for await (const event of run.events) {
  if (event.type === 'completionDone' && event.stopReason === 'error') {
    throw new Error(event.error?.message || 'Inference failed')
  }
  if (event.type === 'contentDelta') text += event.text
}
```

QVAC 0.21 rejects `n_discarded`; manage bounded history and overflow in the app. The maintained scaffold checks device type before model load. Its `EXPO_PUBLIC_QVAC_MOCK=1` path echoes text and does not call native inference.

## Acceptance

Install, bare-pack, Expo prebuild and native compilation must pass before testing runtime. On a simulator verify worker startup, KV persistence and optional mock chat. Real inference requires a physical device according to QVAC documentation. Do not equate a mock result, successful build or SDK bundle verification with real mobile inference. Keep Android and physical-device claims pending until their own evidence exists.
